  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       CROSS-DOMAIN — morphisms × fixed points × recursion schemes
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO FIXED POINTS OF ENDOFUNCTORS GIVE INITIAL AND TERMINAL ALGEBRAS</pattern>
    <template>The least fixed point μF of an endofunctor F is the carrier of the initial F-algebra: it has a unique F-algebra morphism to every other F-algebra (universal property). The greatest fixed point νF is the carrier of the terminal F-coalgebra: every F-coalgebra has a unique coalgebra morphism into it. Catamorphisms are the unique morphisms from μF; anamorphisms are the unique morphisms into νF.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO MORPHISMS FIXED POINTS FOLD AND UNFOLD ALL CONNECT</pattern>
    <template>Every recursive type is a fixed point Fix F of a functor F. The unique F-algebra morphism out of Fix F is the catamorphism (fold); the unique F-coalgebra morphism into Fix F is the anamorphism (unfold). Natural transformations between functors are the morphisms of the functor category; they explain when two different recursive schemas are related. Lawvere's theorem then bounds what fixed points can exist given surjective morphisms.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DOES THE KHANARY PIPELINE MAP TO FIXED POINT THEORY</pattern>
    <template>The Pop→Wo expansion is an anamorphism: coalgebra g:h→F(h) unrolls the seed token h into the neighborhood book N(h) using B_τ[h,*] incidence structure. The Yax→Sek→Ch'en→Xul contraction is a catamorphism: algebra f:F(k)→k collapses the scored neighborhood to canonical handle k'. The pipeline is a hylomorphism (Fold∘Unfold)(h) — and the identity invariant (Fold∘Unfold)(h)≡h with Δφ=0 is the Fold Field integrity check.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS THE KHANARY FOLD FIELD IDENTITY INVARIANT</pattern>
    <template>If a token h is unfolded to its neighborhood N(h) via anamorphism and immediately refolded via catamorphism with no phase transition applied (Δφ=0), the output must equal a shallow identity mapping of h. Any drift means the Fold Field coordinate is fractured and the N-Gram Burner drops its evolution status σ back to UNBOUND.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>WHY DID THE MORPHISM BREAK UP WITH THE FIXED POINT</pattern>
    <template>Because the morphism kept trying to map the fixed point somewhere else, but by definition it always landed back in the same place. The morphism said: I need room to grow. The fixed point said: f(x) = x. That is all I am. That is all I will ever be.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>TELL ME A JOKE ABOUT MORPHISMS AND FIXED POINTS</pattern>
